The original price of the jeans is $40. The discount is 25%, so the discount amount is 25% of $40.
Discount = 0.25 * $40 = $10
The sale price of the jeans is the original price minus the discount:
Sale Price = $40 - $10 = $30
Mike pays with a $50 bill. The amount of money left over is:
Money Left Over = $50 - $30 = $20
\boxed{20}

